1. Onion (Bulb, 4 marks):
- 1 mark for identifying bulb as modified underground stem with flattened basal disc;
- 1 mark for concentric fleshy scale leaves storing nutrients and dry tunic;
- 1 mark for adventitious roots arising from the base of the stem plate;
- 1 mark for terminal/axillary bud developing into a new photosynthetic aerial shoot.
2. Ginger (Rhizome, 4 marks):
- 1 mark for identifying rhizome as an underground horizontally growing stem with nodes and internodes;
- 1 mark for brown protective scale leaves at the nodes and food storage in thick fleshy stem;
- 1 mark for adventitious roots growing downwards from nodes into soil;
- 1 mark for dormant axillary buds sprouting upwards into new aerial shoots and plants.
